        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The 7.0 AT solves a real problem that almost nobody else at this price has bothered to
            solve. <strong class="text-white">Dial controls plus a motor tuned to reach the new
            speed quickly</strong> means an interval session can be executed as written rather than
            approximated — and a 60-inch deck and 3.0 CHP motor make it a good treadmill besides.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy it if your training involves changing pace. If you run at one speed, buy
            <a href="/sole-f63-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">something heavier and plainer</a>
            for the same money. If you mostly walk, buy
